{"title":"1968 AHSME Problems/Problem 20","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The measures of the interior angles of a convex polygon of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> sides are in arithmetic progression. If the common difference is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/e/a4e94a4d2b45632cf823bb8c26eb19aec5c70cd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> and the largest angle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/e/ece184b486bcd76cff4e781214deef445d299dbb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$160^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"33\" height=\"13\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> equals:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/c/55ca5a005956f081083f3b5a5b220b0bf95a8575.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A) } 9\\quad \\text{(B) } 10\\quad \\text{(C) } 12\\quad \\text{(D) } 16\\quad \\text{(E) } 32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"300\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The formula for the sum of the angles in any polygon is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/e/a5eccfe73a52885542fe472750d0ea086d9b33eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180(n-2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"85\" height=\"20\" />. Because this particular polygon is convex and has its angles in an arithmetic sequence with its largest angle being <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/2/b921eebe6fcb6019117772839fa2aa142827e703.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$160$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, we can find the sum of the angles.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/b/88bd4d846cba24ae66ccf7d55663cf514c0905a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n}=160$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"69\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/8/dc8624ebed7ec556f07557d70b0b13d243ceedb4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{1}=160-5(n-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"154\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Plugging this into the formula for finding the sum of an arithmetic sequence...\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/6/0c6778e0eafd57d694d6564151089c48c82793fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\left(\\frac{160+160-5(n-1)}{2}\\right)=180(n-2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"318\" height=\"45\" />.\n</p><p>Simplifying, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/4/264a6d8e34e5fec5aa09cb41bcf7fc7fe03e6876.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2+7n-144$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"110\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Since we want the positive solution to the quadratic, we can easily factor and find the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/e/ebe079776243b0c3fa9b7529c08a3cfc0df71083.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=\\boxed{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"56\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>Hence the answer is<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/6/386255c1da145bc497cf598169ccbaa210e8d0cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\fbox{A}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"24\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME\" title=\"1968 AHSME\">1968 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1968 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1968 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1968\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"1968 AHSME Problems/Problem 19\">Problem 19</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"1968 AHSME Problems/Problem 21\">Problem 21</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1968 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1968 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1968 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4